\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-29\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>. To do this, we will find the zeros of the expression inside the absolute value:\n<br><br>\n<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"15.518ex\" height=\"2.072ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -833.9 6859 915.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D465\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D465\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(605,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1230.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(2231,0)\"><use data-c=\"35\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-35\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2731,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D465\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D465\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(3525.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(4525.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"36\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-36\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(5303.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(6359,0)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>\n<br><br>\nSolving this quadratic equation, we find that the zeros are <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"5.442ex\" height=\"1.532ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -666 2405.6 677\" xmlns:xlink=\